{
  "requirement": "A skill that needs a topic whose home under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure` is another skill MUST refer to that skill instead of restating the topic. It MAY summarize the topic in a few lines.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.cli.skill_structure.refer` has two testable obligations:\n\n1. **Refer to the home.** A skill that needs a topic whose home is another skill MUST refer to that skill.\n2. **Do not restate.** The skill MUST NOT restate the topic. It MAY summarize it in a few lines, which is optional and needs no check.\n\nBoth are covered by `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_refer_to_a_topic_home_instead_of_restating_it]`, which is marked `{test}` for the subject.\n\n- **Referral.** The test loops over all five bundled skills (`habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `habeas-refactor`).\n  - For each skill it calls `assert_phrases`, which collapses the skill's `SKILL.md` and `references/` files with `bundled_skill` and asserts that each phrase appears.\n  - The phrases are concrete pointers to another skill's home. Examples: \"the habeas-evidence skill's `references/fixme.md`\"; \"\\\"Choosing references\\\" in the habeas-requirements skill\"; \"the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`\"; \"under the habeas-requirements skill\".\n  - Every skill has at least three such pointers, so cross-skill referral is asserted for each skill.\n- **No restating.** For each skill, the test then loops over every other skill and calls `home_markers(home)`.\n  - These are verbatim phrases that state part of a topic in full. Examples: \"A judgment is one of three outcomes\"; \"`habeas refactor --dry-run`\"; \"## What the review checks\"; \"| Task | Skill |\".\n  - The test asserts that none of them appears in the skill under test. A skill that copied another home's full statement would fail with \"{name} restates {marker:?}\".\n  - `home_markers` covers all five skills as homes, and the `_` arm panics on an unknown skill.\n\nLimits of this check:\n\n- The no-restating check only catches verbatim copies of the listed markers. A paraphrased restatement would pass.\n- A phrase-based test is the practical way to check this prose requirement, and the markers are distinctive per topic.\n- The \"MAY summarize\" clause permits behavior and needs no test.\n- The home of each topic is defined by the cited parent `requirements.cli.skill_structure` and the per-skill refinements. Those are tested by their own tests and are not reassessed here.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "6115c62c4b082726b08c9d70071d703ebc910924401de32d17d18c54548601b3",
